-- title:
--   A G-invariant chart element avoiding all Igusa valuation rings
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $q$ and $\ell'$, a nonzero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places (valuation subrings containing the constants, proper and with principal ideals) of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ generated over the residue field of $A$ by the Laurent expansions $j(\mathsf q)$ and $j(\mathsf q^{M'})$, a distinguished $s \in W$, an inclusion $hle$ of the base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field into the level-$\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ field $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and a constant reduction $R_0$ of that base-changed field along $A$ onto the said field over the residue field of $A$. Fix further an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, elements $\pi_0$ (with image in $A$), $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $\xi$ of $k_0$, a natural number $\ell$, an intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with a valuation subring $A_b$ cut out by $A$ and an element $\varpi_b$ of it, an intermediate field $K_{\ell}$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ over $k_0$ which is an algebra over $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ compatibly with $k_0$, a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$, an element $\varpi_t' \in A_0$, an ideal $y$ of the chart algebra of elements of $K_\ell$ integral over $A_0[j_\ell]$, an $A_0$-subalgebra $B_t \subseteq K_\ell$ contained in a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$, natural numbers $n, m$, an element $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal, a proof $hjK$ that $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$ lies in $K_\ell$, an element $a_0 \in A_0$, a finite set $ends$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, and a bundle $\mathcal F$ of the rigid-descent hypotheses `RigidDescentHyps` attached to all these data. Let $G$ be the subgroup of $\mathrm{Aut}_{k_0}(K_\ell)$ generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}$ for $\gamma^{-1}$ at level $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with parameters $n = m = q\ell'$ and root of unity $\xi$, that is: for all weights $k$ and all modular forms $f,g$ of that level with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ giving a nonzero series, every $x \in K_\ell$ whose Laurent series is the quotient of those of $p_f$ and $p_g$, and every ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell')\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell')\gamma^{-1}$. Let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ be the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K_\ell$ consisting of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ of elements lying in $W_t$. The assertion is that there exists $b \in K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$ and which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the following properties: the constants of $V$ are exactly $A$, in the sense that for $x \in k_0$ one has $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $K_0$ lies in $V$; if the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $V$ then it lies in the maximal ideal of $V$; and, whenever $j^\sharp := \mathrm{qExpand}_{\ell'}$ of the $k_0$-coefficient image of the Laurent expansion $j(\mathsf q)$ lies in $K_\ell$, in $K_0$ and in $V$, the element $j^\sharp$ is residually transcendental over the constants, in the sense that for every monic polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(j^\sharp)$ lies in $V$ then it is not in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   This is the step of the rigid descent from level $q\ell'$ to the fixed field $K_0$ of the group of level automorphisms: an element of the rigid chart algebra $B_t$ with a pole along every Igusa-type valuation of $K_\ell$ is replaced by a $G$-invariant one in $B_0 \subseteq K_0$ retaining that property, the Igusa test being read on $j^\sharp = j(\mathsf q^{\ell'})$. It is used in the assembly of the semistable supersingular chart data, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_poles_moduliHasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_deckSep_linkedScalars_linkedInertia_of_rigidChart).
